 ## 16. Parity plan
 
-L3 is out of scope. A reimplementation is judged on V-1 through V-8. **V-8 is the one that decides the shape of the port**: the advance belongs outside the handlers, and a handler expresses "jump", "wait" or "return" by pre-subtracting. **V-4 is the one to test
-first** — raising on an unknown opcode is the obvious behaviour and it breaks six valid ones. **V-5
-is the one not to "fix"**: aligning the pre-decode threshold with the length band changes nothing
-observable, but separating the two without noticing they disagree introduces an overread.
+L3 implementation remains later. Tests of database sufficiency should preserve actual PC/phase/
+scratch transitions, stack disposal, result typing and target ownership. Do not introduce a fresh
+per-call stack lifetime, three-frame command phasing, universal PC advancement or guaranteed result
+append. Extend the original-code slice into remaining opcode/wait mechanisms with explicit inputs
+and discriminating controls; do not rerun settled cases merely to inflate counts.
 
